  "status_text": "Three people can vote on eight possibilities, and even the smallest circuit takes forty-four gates to tell whether the number of winners is odd. Give each voter a yes-or-no card for each setting of three switches. A setting wins if all three say yes. Two AND gates check each setting. To combine two results, ask whether they differ. Seven of those comparisons give the final answer. At 21:35 UTC Lean checked that 44 is optimal with AND, OR and NOT, at most two wires per gate. The exact cost extends to n voters and n switches when each voter sees the whole setting (L-clb-120).",
